{"step_index":864,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:04:42Z","input_tokens":2640,"cache_read_tokens":43890,"output_tokens":1385,"content":"### Table Column Alignment & Post-Processing Swap Fix Completed\n\nThe invoice parser has been updated across both the **FastAPI Python backend** and the **JavaScript client engine** to resolve column alignment issues and prevent quantity/rate swaps.\n\n---\n\n### Key Implementations\n\n#### 1. Gemini Extraction Prompt Updated\nAdded table-parsing and column-boundary alignment rules to `TABLE COLUMN ALIGNMENT INSTRUCTIONS` in [server.py](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/server.py#L102-L107) and [utils/aiExtractor.js](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/aiExtractor.js#L20-L29):\n- **Column Boundaries:** Locates column headers (`S.No`, `Description`, `HSN/SAC`, `Quantity`, `Unit`, `Rate/Price`, `Amount`).\n- **Internal Cross-Checking:** Verifies that $\\text{quantity} \\times \\text{unit\\_rate} \\approx \\text{total\\_amount}$. Warns against mistaking S.No/HSN/Code for Quantity.\n- **Trivial Rate Prevention:** Forbids assigning rate `1` or `2` to expensive equipment (e.g. `Tool Kit`).\n- **Unit Stripping:** Trims packaging abbreviations like `NO`, `NOS`, `PCS`, `PKT`, `SET` from product descriptions.\n\n#### 2. Post-Processing Column Swap Fallback\nImplemented the column swap check and unit sanitizer across backend and frontend layers:\n- [server.py](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/server.py#L134-L148):\n  ```python\n  for item in items:\n      qty = item.get('quantity', 0)\n      rate = item.get('unit_rate', 0)\n      total = item.get('total_amount', 0)\n      \n      # If total matches qty exactly and rate is small (e.g. qty=535, rate=2, total=535), \n      # it means qty and rate were misaligned. Swap them:\n      if total > 0 and qty == total and rate in [1, 2, 1.0, 2.0]:\n          item['quantity'] = 1.0\n          item['unit_rate'] = total\n  ```\n- [utils/clean_items.py](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/clean_items.py#L61-L71): Applied in `clean_extracted_items()` and `sanitize_invoice_data()`.\n- [utils/itemCleaner.js](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/itemCleaner.js#L64-L71) & [utils/privacyMasker.js](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/privacyMasker.js#L94-L99): Matches client-side parsing pipeline.\n\n---\n\n### Verification Results\n\nA unit test was executed against the API with an inverted input:\n```json\n{\n  \"description\": \"Heavy Duty Tool Kit NOS\",\n  \"quantity\": 535,\n  \"unit_rate\": 2,\n  \"total_amount\": 535.0\n}\n```\n\n**Normalized Output:**\n- `description`: `\"Heavy Duty Tool Kit\"` (trailing unit `NOS` trimmed)\n- `quantity`: `1.0`\n- `unit_rate`: `535.0`\n- `total_amount`: `535.0`\n\nThe FastAPI server is active and serving the application at `http://localhost:3000`.","thinking":"All user instructions have been implemented and verified. The final response will detail the table column alignment instructions integrated into both the backend (Python) and frontend (JavaScript) extraction processes.\n\n\n"}
{"step_index":865,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:12:05Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nCRITICAL FIX FOR INVOICE EXTRACTION & MATH AUDIT ENGINE:\n\nFix the OCR parsing, comma handling, garbage line-item filtering, and grand total extraction across the backend:\n\n1. UPDATE THE GEMINI EXTRACTION PROMPT:\nReplace the system prompt with these strict rules:\n\n\"You are an Indian GST Tax Invoice extractor. Your job is to extract exact numbers and text without dropping digits or inventing items.\n\nCRITICAL RULES:\n1. COMMA & NUMBER HANDLING (DO NOT DROP DIGITS):\n   - In Indian currency notation, commas are thousands separators. NEVER drop digits before commas!\n   - Example: '2,535.00' is 2535.0 (Two Thousand Five Hundred Thirty-Five), NOT 535.\n   - Example: '1,270.00' is 1270.0 (One Thousand Two Hundred Seventy), NOT 270.\n   - Always verify extracted figures against the printed 'Amount/Total in Words' (e.g., 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES ONLY' means the total is 4490, not 2173).\n\n2. ONLY REAL PRODUCTS/SERVICES IN LINE ITEMS:\n   - Extract ONLY genuine products or services from the central invoice table (e.g., 'Bosch All-in-One Metal Hand Tool Kit', 'Taparia Universal Tool Kit').\n   - Clean the product description: strip table borders, brackets, or leading/trailing symbols like '[', '|', ']', or unit words like 'NOS'/'PCS'.\n   - NEVER extract rubber stamps, signatures, authorization seals, or hand scribbles (e.g., symbols like '©', '~', '|', '[', ']').\n\n3. GRAND TOTAL EXTRACTION:\n   - Look strictly for the final 'Grand Total', 'Total Amount', 'Net Payable', or 'कुल योग' at the bottom of the invoice (e.g., 4,490.00).\n   - DO NOT hallucinate the grand total by summing OCR misreads. Extract the actual printed total on the invoice.\n\n4. COLUMN INTEGRITY:\n   - Quantity is typically an integer (e.g., 1, 2, 5).\n   - Rate is the unit price (e.g., 2535.00, 1270.00).\n   - Billed Amount must reflect (Quantity * Unit Rate).\"\n\n2. BACKEND POST-PROCESSING & SANITIZATION (Python):\nAdd/update this cleaning function to run on the extracted JSON before sending it to the frontend:\n\nimport re\n\ndef sanitize_and_clean_invoice(data: dict) -> dict:\n    # 1. Clean supplier name of trailing symbols\n    if data.get(\"vendor_name\"):\n        data[\"vendor_name\"] = re.sub(r'[\\s&0\\|\\[\\]\\(\\)]+$', '', data[\"vendor_name\"]).strip()\n\n    # 2. Filter garbage line items\n    clean_items = []\n    for item in data.get(\"items\", []):\n        desc = (item.get(\"description\") or \"\").strip()\n        \n        # Remove stray leading/trailing brackets and vertical pipes from OCR\n        desc = re.sub(r'^[\\[\\|\\]\\(\\)\\s]+|[\\[\\|\\]\\(\\)\\s]+$', '', desc).strip()\n        item[\"description\"] = desc\n\n        # Skip if description lacks at least 4 letters\n        if len(re.findall(r'[a-zA-Z]', desc)) < 4:\n            continue\n\n        # Skip if more than 20% of description is weird symbols/punctuation\n        symbols = re.findall(r'[~|©\\[\\]=_{}@#$%^&*]', desc)\n        if len(desc) > 0 and (len(symbols) / len(desc)) > 0.20:\n            continue\n\n        # Skip common footer/stamp terms\n        if any(term in desc.lower() for term in [\"signature\", \"authorised\", \"terms\", \"condition\", \"bank details\"]):\n            continue\n\n        # Quantity and Rate sanity\n        qty = float(item.get(\"quantity\") or 1)\n        rate = float(str(item.get(\"unit_rate\") or 0).replace(\",\", \"\"))\n        billed = float(str(item.get(\"total_amount\") or (qty * rate)).replace(\",\", \"\"))\n\n        item[\"quantity\"] = qty\n        item[\"unit_rate\"] = rate\n        item[\"total_amount\"] = billed\n        clean_items.append(item)\n\n    data[\"items\"] = clean_items\n\n    # 3. Ensure numeric fields strip commas cleanly\n    for key in [\"subtotal\", \"cgst\", \"sgst\", \"igst\", \"declared_total\"]:\n        if data.get(key) is not None:\n            data[key] = float(str(data[key]).replace(\",\", \"\").strip())\n\n    return data\n\nApply `sanitize_and_clean_invoice` to all Gemini outputs before updating the UI state.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-02T23:42:05+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":866,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:12:05Z","input_tokens":49133,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1321,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nInitial focus is on data extraction rules from invoices. Need to handle numbers with commas as thousands separators, removing them before parsing. Verification against \"Amount in Words\" is crucial to avoid misinterpretations. Also, only actual products/services should be extracted from the invoice table, with cleaning to remove extraneous characters.\n\nGrand totals must be extracted directly from the invoice and not calculated from other line items. Ensuring data integrity involves checking that quantities are integers, rates are unit prices, and billed amounts are consistent with quantity and rate. Finally, a backend cleaning function is needed to sanitize the extracted JSON.\n\n\nVendor names require cleaning to remove trailing symbols and whitespace. Line items need filtering: descriptions shorter than four letters or with excessive special characters should be discarded. Further filtering removes items containing common footer terms. The quantity and rate fields are being sanitized.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":160,"Path":"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/server.py","StartLine":80}}]}
{"step_index":867,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:12:15Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-02T23:42:15+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-02T23:42:15+05:30\nShowing lines 80-160 of 211\n80: \n81: @app.post(\"/api/analyze-bill\")\n82: async def analyze_bill(\n83:     file: UploadFile = File(...),\n84:     x_api_key: Optional[str] = Header(None, alias=\"x-api-key\")\n85: ):\n86:     contents = await file.read()\n87:     mime_type = file.content_type or \"image/jpeg\"\n88:     \n89:     # Prompt with table column alignment instructions\n90:     prompt = \"\"\"Extract the invoice details from this image/document into JSON:\n91:  - vendor_name: (string)\n92:  - gstin: (string or null)\n93:  - invoice_number: (string or null)\n94:  - items: list of {description, quantity, unit_rate, total_amount}\n95:  - subtotal: (number)\n96:  - cgst: (number)\n97:  - sgst: (number)\n98:  - igst: (number)\n99:  - declared_total: (number)\n100:  If any field is missing or unclear, leave it null. Do not include addresses or phone numbers as line items.\n101: \n102: TABLE COLUMN ALIGNMENT INSTRUCTIONS:\n103: - Carefully identify the table header row to locate column boundaries (S.No, Description, HSN/SAC, Quantity, Unit, Rate/Price, Amount).\n104: - CROSS-CHECK MATH INTERNALLY: For each row, verify that (quantity * unit_rate) roughly equals the row total amount. \n105:   * If quantity * rate does not equal the row amount, you likely swapped the Quantity and Rate columns, or confused the Item Code/HSN/S.No with Quantity. \n106:   * Never set Rate to trivial numbers like 1 or 2 when the item is an expensive product like a 'Tool Kit', unless that is explicitly the printed unit rate.\n107: - Clean description: Do not append units like 'NO', 'PCS', 'NOS', or serial numbers into the product description.\"\"\"\n108: \n109:     genai_client = get_genai_client(x_api_key)\n110:     if not genai_client:\n111:         return JSONResponse(\n112:             status_code=400,\n113:             content={\"error\": \"Gemini API key is required.\"}\n114:         )\n115: \n116:     # Call Gemini (primary: gemini-2.5-flash; fallback to gemini-3.5-flash if 404/unavailable)\n117:     models_to_try = ['gemini-2.5-flash', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 'gemini-3.8-flash']\n118:     last_err = None\n119: \n120:     for model_name in models_to_try:\n121:         try:\n122:             response = genai_client.models.generate_content(\n123:                 model=model_name,\n124:                 contents=[\n125:                     types.Part.from_bytes(data=contents, mime_type=mime_type),\n126:                     prompt\n127:                 ],\n128:                 config=types.GenerateContentConfig(\n129:                     response_mime_type=\"application/json\",\n130:                     response_schema=ExtractedInvoice,\n131:                     temperature=0.0\n132:                 )\n133:             )\n134:             # Post-Processing Column Swap Fallback (Python)\n135:             try:\n136:                 parsed = json.loads(response.text)\n137:                 items = parsed.get(\"items\", [])\n138:                 for item in items:\n139:                     qty = item.get('quantity', 0)\n140:                     rate = item.get('unit_rate', 0)\n141:                     total = item.get('total_amount', 0)\n142:                     \n143:                     # If total matches qty exactly and rate is small (e.g. qty=535, rate=2, total=535), \n144:                     # it means qty and rate were misaligned. Swap them:\n145:                     if total > 0 and qty == total and rate in [1, 2, 1.0, 2.0]:\n146:                         item['quantity'] = 1.0\n147:                         item['unit_rate'] = total\n148: \n149:                 sanitized = sanitize_invoice_data(parsed)\n150:                 return Response(content=json.dumps(sanitized), media_type=\"application/json\")\n151:             except Exception as e:\n152:                 print(f\"[AUDIT IT] Post-processing note: {e}\")\n153:                 return Response(content=response.text, media_type=\"application/json\")\n154:         except Exception as err:\n155:             last_err = err\n156:             err_str = str(err)\n157:             # If 404 not found (model retired by Google) or 503 spike, try next candidate\n158:             if \"404\" in err_str or \"503\" in err_str or \"not found\" in err_str.lower():\n159:                 print(f\"[AUDIT IT] Model {model_name} unavailable ({err_str[:80]}), trying next...\")\n160:                 continue"}
{"step_index":868,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:12:15Z","input_tokens":2772,"cache_read_tokens":49143,"output_tokens":864,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nFocus is on ensuring accurate extraction of numerical values, particularly the grand total and individual item amounts. Cross-referencing extracted figures with the \"Amount/Total in Words\" field is crucial for validation. The grand total must be directly extracted from the invoice and not calculated from item subtotals. Item extraction focuses on real products/services and eliminates irrelevant data like stamps or symbols.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":50,"Path":"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/clean_items.py","StartLine":1}}]}
{"step_index":869,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:12:23Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-02T23:42:23+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-02T23:42:23+05:30\nShowing lines 1-50 of 229\n1: \"\"\"\n2: AUDIT IT - Item Cleaning & Exclusion Filter\n3: Enforces strict Header vs Table separation and purges metadata from line items.\n4: \"\"\"\n5: \n6: import re\n7: \n8: def clean_extracted_items(items: list) -> list:\n9:     \"\"\"\n10:     Purges metadata, phone numbers, and GSTIN strings from extracted items array.\n11:     Ensures any item containing phone numbers, GSTIN strings, or metadata keywords\n12:     is purged before passing the items to the total recalculation logic.\n13:     \"\"\"\n14:     cleaned = []\n15:     \n16:     # Pattern matching GSTIN (15 characters: 2 digits, 5 letters, 4 digits, 1 letter, 1 digit/letter, Z, 1 digit/letter)\n17:     gstin_pattern = re.compile(r'\\b\\d{2}[A-Z]{5}\\d{4}[A-Z]{1}[1-9A-Z]{1}Z[0-9A-Z]{1}\\b', re.IGNORECASE)\n18:     # Pattern matching Indian phone numbers (10 digits, optional +91 prefix)\n19:     phone_pattern = re.compile(r'(\\+?91[\\-\\s]?)?[6-9]\\d{9}')\n20:     \n21:     # Common metadata keywords that should never be product names\n22:     forbidden_keywords = [\n23:         \"gstin\", \"gst no\", \"contact\", \"phone\", \"mobile\", \"tel\", \n24:         \"pan no\", \"bank\", \"ifsc\", \"account no\", \"invoice no\",\n25:         \"tax invoice\", \"bill to\", \"ship to\", \"address\", \"state code\",\n26:         \"reverse charge\", \"e-way bill\", \"transport\", \"vehicle no\",\n27:         \"cash memo\", \"challan\", \"original for recipient\", \"date\"\n28:     ]\n29: \n30:     for item in items:\n31:         if not item or not isinstance(item, dict):\n32:             continue\n33: \n34:         desc = item.get(\"description\", \"\").strip()\n35:         desc_lower = desc.lower()\n36: \n37:         # 1. Skip if the description contains GSTIN patterns or phone numbers\n38:         if gstin_pattern.search(desc) or phone_pattern.search(desc):\n39:             continue\n40: \n41:         # 2. Skip if the description is just a metadata label\n42:         if any(keyword in desc_lower for keyword in forbidden_keywords):\n43:             continue\n44: \n45:         # 3. Skip invalid items with zero/negative rates or quantities\n46:         qty = item.get(\"quantity\") if item.get(\"quantity\") is not None else item.get(\"qty\", 0)\n47:         rate = item.get(\"unit_rate\") if item.get(\"unit_rate\") is not None else item.get(\"rate\", 0)\n48:         amount = item.get(\"total_amount\") if item.get(\"total_amount\") is not None else item.get(\"amount\", 0)\n49: \n50:         # Ensure numeric values"}
